{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-12841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${(s-t)}^{9}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-12841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+…+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(s-t)}^{9},$ we have  $a=s,$ $b=-t,$ $n=9.$ \n\nTherefore, the first three terms of ${(s-t)}^{9}$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(s-t)}^{9} & =(\\frac{9}{0}){(s)}^{9}{(-t)}^{0}+(\\frac{9}{1}){(s)}^{9-1}{(-t)}^{1}+(\\frac{9}{2}){(s)}^{9-2}{(-t)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =1{(s)}^{9}+9{(s)}^{8}{(-t)}^{1}+36{(s)}^{7}{(-t)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =1({s}^{9})+9({s}^{8})(-t)+36({s}^{7})({t}^{2})+… \\\\  & ={s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t+36{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-12841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c32e00125e549555645a5e5fe28443cc9e59ee63a2fed351a55705e69d8a35"} {"question" "q-12841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-12841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{s}^{9}+9{s}^{8}t+72{s}^{7}t+…"] ["math" "{s}^{9}+9{s}^{8}t-36{s}^{7}t+…"] ["math" "{s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t+36{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…"] ["math" "{s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t+42{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…"] ["math" "{s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t-72{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-12841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t+36{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-18621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The coefficient of ${x}^{22}$ in the expansion of ${(3+{x}^{2})}^{13}$ is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-18621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+…+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(3+{x}^{2})}^{13},$ we have $a=3,$ $b={x}^{2},$ and $n=13.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(3+{x}^{2})}^{13}=(\\frac{13}{0}){3}^{13}{({x}^{2})}^{0}+(\\frac{13}{1}){3}^{13-1}{({x}^{2})}^{1}+(\\frac{13}{2}){3}^{13-2}{({x}^{2})}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{13}{13}){3}^{13-13}{({x}^{2})}^{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${x}^{22}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{13}{11}){3}^{13-11}{({x}^{2})}^{11}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying this term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{13}{11}){3}^{13-11}{({x}^{2})}^{11} & =78\\cdot {3}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{22} \\\\  & =78\\cdot 9\\cdot {x}^{22} \\\\  & =702{x}^{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{22}$ is $702.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-18621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c32e00125e549555645a5e5fe28443cc9e59ee63a2fed351a55705e69d8a35"} {"question" "q-18621" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-18621" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "512"] ["math" "560"] ["math" "702"] ["math" "880"] ["math" "908"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-18621" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "702"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-113627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The coefficient of ${x}^{7}$ in the expansion of ${(4+x)}^{9}$ is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-113627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(4+x)}^{9},$ we have $a=4,$ $b=x,$ and $n=9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4+x)^{9}=(\\frac{9}{0}){4}^{9}{x}^{0}+(\\frac{9}{1}){4}^{9-1}{x}^{1}+(\\frac{9}{2}){4}^{9-2}{x}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{9}{9}){4}^{9-9}{x}^{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${x}^{7}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{9}{7}){4}^{9-7}{x}^{7}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the coefficient, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{9}{7}){4}^{9-7} & =36\\cdot {4}^{2} \\\\  & =36\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =576.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{7}$ is $576.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-113627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0c32e00125e549555645a5e5fe28443cc9e59ee63a2fed351a55705e69d8a35"} {"question" "q-113627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005387/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d7138b093771f45ed73de72481a6b16ed6847fe4d1f43bf8f1bf8ceadce2183"} {"question" "q-113627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "144"] ["math" "1\\,152"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "576"] ["math" "72"]] "categor